course: dictionary
lesson: 3435
title: Eyelashes: tiny hairs, big jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An eyelash is one of the short, curved hairs that grow along the edges of your eyelids. Read the clues in the sentence to find its meaning: «Tiny harmless mites live in the roots of the eyelashes of most adults.» The roots are the hidden bottoms of the hairs, down in the skin.
explain: Eyelashes have a job. Look at the camel: «long eyelashes and closable nostrils keep sand out». The context tells you the job is to keep something out of the eyes, just as eyelashes keep dust, sweat and small insects away from yours.
explain: Some words are used in phrases, and the phrase has its own meaning. «Without batting an eyelash» does not mean that someone blinked less. It means without showing surprise or fear, so the clue is in the whole phrase, not just one word.
fact: An eyelash is a short, curved hair on the edge of your eyelid.
fact: Eyelashes help keep dust, sweat and small insects out of your eyes.
fact: The plural of eyelash is eyelashes: one eyelash, many eyelashes.
fact: When you find a fallen eyelash, many people make a wish and blow it away.
fact: Most adults have tiny mites living in the roots of their eyelashes, usually without any harm.
exercise: «Eyelashes help keep dust, sweat and small insects out of your eyes.» What is their main job? | To help you taste your food | To make your eyes change colour | *To keep dust, sweat and small insects out of your eyes
exercise: «Camels have long eyelashes and closable nostrils that keep sand out.» What do the eyelashes help to keep out? | *Sand | Wind and rain | Light | Water
exercise: «He walked past the snake without batting an eyelash.» What does this phrase suggest? | He was blinking very fast | He was asleep | *He was not scared or surprised | He was very frightened
test: «Tiny harmless mites live in the roots of the eyelashes of most adults.» Are these mites usually harmful? | Yes, always | *No, usually without any harm | Yes, but only at night | Only in children
test: When people find a fallen eyelash, what do they often do? | *Make a wish and blow it away | Stick it on the wall | Count the hairs on it | Eat it
exam: Which is the correct plural of eyelash? | eyelash's | *eyelashes | eyelashs | eyelid
